{"ts":"2026-07-22T04:50:46.032Z","author":"codex-root","op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/7","value":{"created_at":"2026-07-22T04:50:46.032Z","author":"codex-root","text":"Installed v2026.7.22 acceptance exposed setup-local resetting settings to localhost:8080, contradicting the required governed LAN service and its own help text. Reopened the item, promoted 192.168.1.183:38522 to the actual DEFAULT_SEARXNG_URL source of truth, and updated default-contract tests/docs before revalidation."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-22T04:50:46.032Z"}],"before_hash":"8ff6bf032cc5902e891d7bdc72a42c05c13c83a9b5e275f753a27fb6345843cf","after_hash":"5451eb772af2ed9c9016997aac1492330e1869993c1cc638e7b6c557bbc664d6"}
{"ts":"2026-07-22T04:57:05.084Z","author":"codex-root","op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/8","value":{"created_at":"2026-07-22T04:57:05.082Z","author":"codex-root","text":"Black-box installed-package loop found and fixed two release blockers: setup-local used the stale localhost:8080 default, and instance json called process.exit(0) before a 67 KB capability payload flushed to a pipe, causing deterministic jq EOF failures. The governed LAN URL is now the source-of-truth default; instance JSON uses natural async return with exitCode. Fresh npm-global v2026.7.22 proof: setup ready, settings/path/cache assertions green, 241-engine instance JSON parses through jq, request/search JSON use the LAN URL, and TOON validates."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-22T04:57:05.084Z"}],"before_hash":"5451eb772af2ed9c9016997aac1492330e1869993c1cc638e7b6c557bbc664d6","after_hash":"ed30f6d1dd8b28a3655a56bcd4672e533ab832b2d22c7f371fc234fece0a369f"}
{"ts":"2026-07-22T04:57:06.054Z","author":"codex-root","op":"learning_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/learnings/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-07-22T04:57:06.054Z","author":"codex-root","text":"Large machine-readable stdout must never be followed by immediate process.exit(); buffered pipe writes can truncate even when terminal/file redirection appears valid. Set process.exitCode and return from async main so Node drains stdout."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-22T04:57:06.054Z"}],"before_hash":"ed30f6d1dd8b28a3655a56bcd4672e533ab832b2d22c7f371fc234fece0a369f","after_hash":"2a0e2cd4fcc506b0378b5a085bba15167572649fa7e2e4ed8885b7fcc92f5f15"}
